{"term":"resolve","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:c8373584f6458763ba","definition":"To find a solution to (a problem).","example":"Exeter. Shall I call in Thambaſſadors my Liege? / King. Not yet my Couſin, til we be reſolude / Of ſome ſerious matters touching vs and France.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["decipher","upsolve","work out","absolve","decipher","get to the bottom of","iron out","meliorate","puzzle out","ravel","reason out","resolve","riddle","sleuth","solve","tease out","think out","unpuzzle","unravel","unriddle","unsolve","upsolve","work out","Any from Thesaurus:untangle"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["misresolve","preresolve","proresolving","reresolve","resolvability","resolvable","resolvase","resolvend","resolver","self-resolving","superresolve","time-resolved","unresolve"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resolve#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9f485d1f86324259a1","definition":"To reduce to simple or intelligible notions; to make clear or certain; to unravel; to explain.","example":"to resolve a riddle","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["misresolve","preresolve","proresolving","reresolve","resolvability","resolvable","resolvase","resolvend","resolver","self-resolving","superresolve","time-resolved","unresolve"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resolve#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7f9599354a408ccbbf","definition":"To make a firm decision to do something. To become determined to reach a certain goal or take a certain action.","example":"I resolve to finish this work before I go home.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["misreso